Ported (TypeScript to Rust) into crates/kgraf-orchestrator/src/verify.rs:
the per-attempt (ray) lifecycle `empty | scattering | success | stopped |
error`; one cancellation per attempt, so stopping one never touches another;
`messageWasInterruptedAtStart`, an attempt stopped before any content is
empty (no candidate), not failed; and the `playNice` throttle as
`OrchestratorConfig::max_parallel_attempts`.

Not taken: Beam's fusion (a model merging answers). The owner excluded it,
and decision 0009 selects among attempts by verifier. Selection here is the
passing candidate with the lowest spend, then the earliest.
